    "title": "Codi Heuer, ex-Fossil Ridge pitcher, appears in MiLB game on June 23",
    "text": "Former Fossil Ridge High School pitcher Codi Heuer took the mound for the Columbus Clippers during their Minor League Baseball game against the Omaha Storm Chasers on Tuesday, June 23, at 8:05 p.m. The Clippers lost the contest 3-2.\nThe matchup was played at Werner Park and marked the seventh time the two teams faced each other this year. The Clippers currently lead the season series 4-3 over the Storm Chasers.\nHeuer pitched 1 inning and recorded 1 strikeout.\nThe Clippers are set to play the Storm Chasers again at Werner Park on Wednesday, June 24.\nCodi Heuer — Pitcher — 6â€²5â€³ — 200 — Hometown: Missoula",
